  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- New module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/tab_clear.rs`. After each ring's tabs are fitted, it reads each tab's line on the ring against every other cut of the tabbed levels. The other cuts are: the other keeps of the same ring, the far part of the two keeps beside the tab, and every other ring.\r\n- A cut nearer than the tool diameter `D` cuts into the tab. The loop is held: its tabbed levels cut nothing. A `tabs:` note names the tab and the distance.\r\n- A cut between `D` and `W + D` away leaves the tab at its width. A `tabs:` note names the tab and the width of the strip beside it. The moves do not change.\r\n- `tab_bridge.rs`: a `tabs:` note when the first tab grows back over a picked start. The note names the pick and the point where the tabbed levels start.\r\n- `contour.rs`: one line. The fits of all rings are made before the level loop.\r\n- No posted move changes for a program that gets no new note.\r\n\r\n## Cause\r\n\r\nThe bridge check compared only the two cuts beside a tab. It read the last `W + D` of one walk and the first `W + D` of the next walk. A later run of the same ring, or a different ring, was not read.\r\n\r\n## Shape-mask result (on upstream/main `1ae4d061f`)\r\n\r\nTool 6 mm, tab width 4 mm, outside contour, no leads, 0.1 mm grid.\r\n\r\n| Case | Distance between the two cuts | Neck of the tab | Note before |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| U-turn, 10 mm notch | 4 mm | 0.00 mm | none |\r\n| U-turn, 14 mm notch | 8 mm | 1.89 mm | none |\r\n| Second ring, parts 10 mm apart | 4 mm | 0.00 mm and 0.74 mm | none |\r\n| Second ring, parts 14 mm apart | 8 mm | 1.89 mm | none |\r\n\r\nA bridge is narrower than the tab width, so the issue is now `P1`.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\nPins in `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_necks.rs` (new) and `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_bridge.rs`:\r\n\r\n- `a_tab_that_a_u_turn_of_its_ring_cuts_into_holds_the_loop`\r\n- `a_tab_that_a_second_ring_cuts_into_holds_the_loop`\r\n- `a_tab_beside_a_narrow_strip_is_named`\r\n- `a_tab_with_room_beside_it_has_no_note`\r\n- `the_meter_reads_the_tab_width_on_a_plain_part`\r\n- `a_tab_that_grows_over_a_picked_start_says_so`\r\n- `every_tabbed_level_keeps_the_tab_width` (three tabbed levels)\r\n- `the_bridge_holds_on_the_true_arcs_to_a_tenth_of_a_micron`\r\n\r\nMutation results:\r\n\r\n- Old `contour.rs` (from `upstream/main`): the U-turn pin, the second-ring pin and the strip pin are red. The meter reads necks of 0.0 mm. With the fix they are green.\r\n- `moved_start` returns no note: `a_tab_that_grows_over_a_picked_start_says_so` is red. With the fix it is green.\r\n- `every_tabbed_level_keeps_the_tab_width` and `the_bridge_holds_on_the_true_arcs_to_a_tenth_of_a_micron` add coverage. They are green on unchanged code too.\r\n\r\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green, 160 steps, 0 failed, 41 min. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\r\n\r\nThe tab neck meter is `crates/motion/tests/common/tab_neck.rs`. `shape_mask.rs` has 409 lines, so the meter has its own file.\r\n\r\n## Goldens moved\r\n\r\nNone.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- `SLACK = 1e-6` did not change. A margin grows each tab window on a straight wall and moves the recorded router example program. The test reads the bridge on the posted arcs in chords of `1e-5` mm, and no bridge is under the tab width by more than `1e-4` mm. The decision file gives the bound. The reviewer can ask for the margin.\r\n- `contour.rs` still calls `lead_held` on the first keep when that keep is not at the pick. The new note says that the start moved. A picked start with tabs permits only no lead or a perpendicular lead.\r\n- Inside contours and leads are not in the new neck tests. The reviewer's 60 x 7 mm inside slot was not run. By the rule, its two runs are 2.06 mm apart, which is less than `D`, so the loop is held with the note.\r\n- The check is local to the tab. It does not follow a stock strip that becomes narrow away from the tab.\r\n- The build used no compile cache: `sccache rustc -vV` did not return on this machine. The gate ran with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`.\r\n\r\n## Overlaps\r\n\r\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\r\n\r\n## Review fixes\r\n\r\nCommit `57756c69a` (owner-account takeover, ordered by the maintainer) fixes the two findings of the review of head `edb566d33`:\r\n\r\n- `tab_clear::departed` reads a keep that turns back toward its tab before it is `W + D` away (a shallow notch). With one keep, its leads are read the same way. Pin: `a_tab_that_a_u_turn_in_a_shallow_notch_cuts_into_holds_the_loop`.\r\n- `tab_clear::fit_loops` takes the tabbed levels of each loop from the depth ladder. A ring is read against a tab only when the two rings share a tabbed level. Pin: `a_ring_that_stops_above_the_tabs_does_not_hold_another_loop`.\r\n- Quick gate on the new head: 160 steps, 0 failed. Follow-up: #2734.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nChangelog: Contour tabs: a tab that another cut of the same level cuts into now holds its loop with a `tabs:` note; a narrow strip beside a tab and a start point that a tab covers get a note.\r\n\r\nFixes #2561\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
